From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Mark the assertion-only locals of common_subplan_optimizer.cpp as used

common_subplan_optimizer.cpp declares locals that only D_ASSERT() reads (inserted),
so in a release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, they are unused
and -Wunused-variable or -Wunused-but-set-variable says so. Each is cast
to void after its declaration, which changes no behavior.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/common_subplan_optimizer.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/common_subplan_optimizer.cpp
--- a/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/common_subplan_optimizer.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/common_subplan_optimizer.cpp
@@ -1018,6 +1018,7 @@ public:
 				for (idx_t i = 0; i < old_bindings[subplan_idx].size(); i++) {
 					replacer.replacement_bindings.emplace_back(old_bindings[subplan_idx][i], new_bindings[i]);
 					const auto inserted = generated_binding_map.emplace(new_bindings[i], subplan.canonical_bindings[i]);
+					(void)inserted;
 					D_ASSERT(inserted.second);
 				}
 			}
